<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="162" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Sidecar live verification against dev L2 Worker App Service (localhost sitecontainer binding + per-boot shared-secret header)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-6 -- Integration wiring</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Live verification of a security-sensitive component (Exchange-admin cert capability) against a real dev App Service -- deploy-adjacent, escalation-worthy if verification fails.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>High-blast-radius per parent task instructions (sidecar-adjacent) -- Opus tier for the live-verification judgment calls.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>101, 113, 114, 161</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, sidecar, testing, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Deploy task 114's sidecar image (via task 101's Bicep sitecontainer resource + task 113's Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1) to the dev L2 Worker App Service, and verify live: (1) the sitecontainer binds to localhost:8091 within the shared network namespace and is NOT reachable from the public internet-facing surface; (2) task 161's ExchangePolicySidecarClient can reach it and complete a round-trip against a REAL (or safely-scoped test) Exchange tenant, exercising Set-ExchangeApplicationAccessPolicy.ps1's actual get-before-set idempotency; (3) the per-boot shared-secret header mechanism functions correctly (a request WITHOUT the header is rejected). This is the first end-to-end proof that the Class-C residual (the one PowerShell-only piece in the entire handler fleet, per DS-1b §0's verified finding) actually works in the deployed topology, not just in isolated unit/contract tests.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer / Azure infrastructure operator. Expert in App Service sitecontainer live verification, localhost-network-namespace isolation confirmation, and Exchange Online app-only policy application verification.</role>

  <goal>A live verification report confirms: the sidecar container is running and healthy on the dev Worker App Service, its port is confirmed NOT publicly reachable (a request to the public hostname:8091 fails/times out), a live ExchangePolicySidecarClient round-trip against a safely-scoped test tenant/policy succeeds with the expected AlreadyCompliant-on-second-run idempotency behavior, and the shared-secret header rejection path is confirmed (an unauthenticated request is refused).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>This is the culminating verification for the entire Option D sidecar design (DS-1b's whole §3), proving the multi-year architectural bet (DS-1b §0's verified finding that NO Graph API exists for Exchange app-only policy management, now or via its designated successor) actually functions once deployed, not merely designed. This project's Wave G-6 exists specifically to close this loop before Wave G-7's T4 probe (task 180) and the final Phase F E2E run (task 186) depend on it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep (task 101's sitecontainer resource)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 (task 113)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/sidecar-live-verification-2026-08.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="101" status="pending">The sitecontainer Bicep resource this deploys onto</dependency>
      <dependency task="113" status="pending">The deploy script used to get the sidecar image running</dependency>
      <dependency task="114" status="pending">The sidecar image itself</dependency>
      <dependency task="161" status="pending">The client this verification exercises end-to-end</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="DS-1b §3">Verify the port is NOT exposed on the app's public front end -- this is a security property, not merely a functional one; a public-reachable sidecar port is a HIGH-severity finding requiring immediate escalation, not a routine bug.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Human Escalation Triggers (root CLAUDE.md §6)">Security-sensitive code verification -- if the shared-secret rejection path does NOT correctly reject an unauthenticated request, STOP and escalate immediately rather than documenting it as a known gap.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Sidecar live verification</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds1b-option-d-hybrid-deep-dive.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read DS-1b §3 in full for the exact verification criteria.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Deploy">Deploy the sidecar image to dev's Worker App Service via task 113's deploy script.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Container health">Confirm the sitecontainer is running (App Service diagnostics/log stream) and listening on 8091.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Public-reachability negative test">Attempt to reach the sidecar's port via the app's PUBLIC hostname -- confirm failure/timeout (proving network-namespace isolation).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Localhost round-trip">From within the Worker's own network context (or via a diagnostic console/Kudu SSH into the main container), POST to http://localhost:8091/apply-policy with a valid shared-secret header against a safely-scoped test tenant/policy; confirm a Success or AlreadyCompliant response.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Idempotency verify">Run the same request TWICE; confirm the second run returns AlreadyCompliant (proving the script's get-before-set idempotency survives the container+HTTP wrapping).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Auth rejection test">Send a request WITHOUT the shared-secret header; confirm it is rejected (not silently processed).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Client integration">Exercise task 161's ExchangePolicySidecarClient itself (not a raw curl) end-to-end against the live sidecar, confirming the C# client's mapping matches the observed live responses.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Report">File a verification report in notes/ documenting all 6 checks' outcomes.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the public-reachability negative test (step 3) shows the sidecar IS reachable from outside the network namespace, STOP IMMEDIATELY and escalate as a HIGH-severity security finding per root CLAUDE.md §6 — this exposes Exchange-admin-capability to the public internet, the exact risk DS-1b §3's whole isolation design exists to prevent.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the auth-rejection test (step 6) shows an unauthenticated request IS processed, STOP IMMEDIATELY and escalate — this is a security-sensitive-code verification failure per root CLAUDE.md §6, not a routine bug to file and move past.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az webapp">log stream / Kudu console access for live verification</tool>
    <tool name="curl">public-reachability negative test + localhost round-trip if console access permits</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="report">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/sidecar-live-verification-2026-08.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The sitecontainer is confirmed running and healthy on the dev Worker App Service.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A request to the sidecar's port via the PUBLIC hostname fails/times out (network-namespace isolation confirmed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A localhost round-trip (with valid shared-secret header) against a safely-scoped test tenant succeeds with the expected Success/AlreadyCompliant outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A SECOND identical request returns AlreadyCompliant, proving get-before-set idempotency survives the container+HTTP wrapping.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A request WITHOUT the shared-secret header is rejected (not processed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">task 161's ExchangePolicySidecarClient, exercised end-to-end against the live sidecar, correctly maps the observed responses onto HandlerResult.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A verification report exists in notes/ documenting all 6 checks.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- N/A, this is verification, not a new component. Extension -- N/A. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- without live verification, the entire Class-C sidecar architecture (the ONE genuinely novel infrastructure component in Option D, per DS-1b's framing of it as a multi-year bet) is unproven outside unit/contract tests; a network-isolation or idempotency defect discovered only during Phase F's E2E run (task 186) would be far more expensive to diagnose and could delay the acceptance-target transition.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
